{
  "//": "The indexes docs/data-model.md §7 requires. Deployed by infra/deploy-rules.sh.",
  "indexes": [
    {
      "//": "Hierarchical pre-filter, then vector search inside the survivors. The array-contains on node_urns cuts the corpus to the handful of chunks that could possibly be relevant before the ANN runs at all — which is why retrieval here is cheap. Dimension is 1536 because Firestore caps vector indexes at 2048 and a naive 3072-dim embedding will not index; use Matryoshka truncation.",
      "collectionGroup": "spec_chunks",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "node_urns",
          "arrayConfig": "CONTAINS"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "embedding",
          "vectorConfig": {
            "dimension": 1536,
            "flat": {}
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "//": "Everything under this node, at any depth, in one query — the materialised path doing its job.",
      "collectionGroup": "spec_nodes",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "path",
          "arrayConfig": "CONTAINS"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "iso14224_level",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "collectionGroup": "nodes",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "path",
          "arrayConfig": "CONTAINS"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "iso14224_level",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "//": "The measured series, newest first. This is what consistent_with(asset.history) reads, and what makes a wear RATE computable rather than just a wear reading.",
      "collectionGroup": "readings",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "key",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "at",
          "order": "DESCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "//": "The same series across every component on a machine.",
      "collectionGroup": "readings",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION_GROUP",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "key",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "at",
          "order": "DESCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "//": "What has been fitted here, and what is fitted here now — `to == null` is the current placement.",
      "collectionGroup": "placements",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION_GROUP",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "position_urn",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "to",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "//": "The job list a dashboard opens on.",
      "collectionGroup": "jobs",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "status",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "started_at",
          "order": "DESCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "//": "The sweep. COLLECTION_GROUP is load-bearing and not a style choice: /tenants/{t}/tasks is a subcollection, so a COLLECTION-scoped index serves queries within ONE tenant only. The sweep is deliberately cross-tenant — one cron for the whole system — which makes it a collection-group query, and without this index it does not run at all. notify_after is a single computed clock (starts at due_at, moves to now+24h after each notification), so the whole query is one equality and one inequality on one field.",
      "collectionGroup": "tasks",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION_GROUP",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "status",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "notify_after",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "//": "A person's task list.",
      "collectionGroup": "tasks",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "assignee_uid",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "status",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "due_at",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "//": "The unclaimed queue. A task assigned to a ROLE has no owner and therefore no calendar event; claiming it is what creates one.",
      "collectionGroup": "tasks",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "assignee_role",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "status",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "due_at",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "//": "The per-component measured series, now that readings are flat. Flat because a nested collection binds a {document=**} wildcard to its OUTER name and silently escapes the server-written list — see specs/2026-08-20-firestore-design.md section 14.5.",
      "collectionGroup": "readings",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "component_id",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "key",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "at",
          "order": "DESCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "//": "The procedure library view.",
      "collectionGroup": "procedures",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "status",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "updated_at",
          "order": "DESCENDING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "//": "The people view.",
      "collectionGroup": "members",
      "queryScope": "COLLECTION",
      "fields": [
        {
          "fieldPath": "role",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        },
        {
          "fieldPath": "display_name",
          "order": "ASCENDING"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "fieldOverrides": []
}
